  "result": "Perfect! All 274 tests pass. I've successfully implemented the late fee calculation:\n\n**Added lateFee(invoice, asOf) to src/reports.js:**\n- Calculates 0.04% of amount due per day overdue\n- Returns 0 if invoice is not overdue (dueDate >= asOf)\n- Formula: fee = balanceDue(invoice) \u00d7 daysOverdue \u00d7 0.0004, rounded using banker's rounding\n- Days overdue = days between dueDate and asOf using daysBetween()\n- Amount due accounts for payments, VAT, discounts, and vouchers via balanceDue()\n- Does not mutate invoice\n\n**Added 16 comprehensive tests covering:**\n- Not yet due invoices (returns 0)\n- Due today (returns 0)\n- One day overdue\n- Multiple days overdue\n- Partially paid invoices (fee based on remaining balance)\n- Fully paid invoices (returns 0)\n- Zero due amount (returns 0)\n- Large amounts overdue\n- Invoices with VAT\n- Invoices with discounts\n- Multiple line items\n- Very small due amounts\n- Edge cases (rounding behavior)\n- Year boundary spanning\n- Complex scenario with VAT, discount, and payment combined\n- Input immutability\n\nExample calculations:\n- Invoice due 2026-10-15, overdue as of 2026-10-31 (16 days), due 10000 cents\n  - lateFee = 10000 \u00d7 16 \u00d7 0.0004 = 64 cents\n- Same invoice but due 5000 cents after payment\n  - lateFee = 5000 \u00d7 16 \u00d7 0.0004 = 32 cents\n\nAll 274 tests passing.",
